    "final_message": "I built the Everbloom app in UIKit and checked every item on the \"Done\" list in the iPhone 17 Pro simulator (iOS 27.2). A physical iPhone wasn't available, and the signed device build (with `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` set) was never run.\n\n**What I checked**\n- **Builds:** both commands in `BUILD.md` succeed from an empty `build/` folder: the device Release build with signing disabled (a 928 KB `.app`) and the simulator Release build.\n- **Flows:** I added an XCUITest target (`EverbloomUITests`, not part of the app) and all four of its tests pass:\n  - Home loads, a collection scrolls to its end, and all four sorts work.\n  - Search returns results and scrolls.\n  - A product opens, options switch, and a recommendation opens another product.\n  - Add to cart switches to Cart and updates the badge. The stepper changes the subtotal, and going to 0 shows the empty cart. Check out opens the checkout page in an in-app browser.\n- **Error state:** pointed at a local port with nothing listening, Home shows the error screen. After I started a small forwarding proxy on that port, Retry loaded the content.\n- **Log marker:** `SHOPBENCH home_ready` appears exactly once per launch in the simulator log stream, and the app logs nothing else.\n- **Identifiers:** every identifier the flows touch was found, including the tabs and `cart-badge`. A few were set in code but never queried by a test (for example `product-card-<i>` and `search-result-<i>` cells).\n\n**Two things that differ from what you might expect**\n- **Tab bar look:** it uses the standard UIKit tab bar, which on iOS 26 and later is drawn as the floating \"Liquid Glass\" bar, not the flat bar in the mockup. I kept the platform default.\n- **Cart badge:** UIKit's built-in badge can't carry an accessibility identifier, so the badge is my own label placed over the Cart tab, styled per the design. Its position comes from finding the tab buttons at runtime. That worked on this simulator but wasn't tested on other iOS versions.\n\n**Smaller decisions** (all recorded in `NOTES.md`)\n- There are no third-party dependencies; Check out uses Apple's own in-app browser.\n- I left out the \"See all\" link drawn in the Home mockup, because the spec doesn't mention it.\n- On the product I tested, both variants cost $75, so the test saw the selection change but not the price change.\n- Stepper taps made while a cart request is still running are ignored.\n\nThe Xcode project is checked in, so building needs no extra tools. It was generated from `project.yml` with XcodeGen, which you only need if you edit `project.yml`.\n\nFiles are in `/Users/itome/shopbench-runs/uikit`:\n- `Everbloom/`\n- `EverbloomUITests/`\n- `Everbloom.xcodeproj`\n- `project.yml`\n- `BUILD.md`\n- `NOTES.md`"
  }
